  "worked_solution": "First, we find the first-order derivative ${f}_{z}(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202z}(\\frac{z}{x+z}) \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{(x+z)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find ${f}_{zx}(x,y,z)$ by differentiating ${f}_{z}(x,y,z)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{zx}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}({f}_{z}(x,y,z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(\\frac{x}{(x+z)^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+z)^{2}-2x(x+z)}{(x+z)^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{z-x}{(x+z)^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${f}_{zxx}(x,y,z)$ by differentiating ${f}_{zx}(x,y,z)$ with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{zxx}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}({f}_{zy}(x,y,z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(\\frac{z-x}{(x+z)^{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{-(x+z)^{3}-3(z-x)(x+z)^{2}}{(x+z)^{6}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(x-2z)}{(x+z)^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate ${f}_{zxx}(x,y,z)$ at $(1,0,1):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{zxx}(1,0,1) & =\\frac{2(1-2(1))}{(1+1)^{4}}=\\frac{-2}{16}=-\\frac{1}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
